WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.001
- [Narrator] In this world on the day

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.043
this video launches,

00:00:02.043 --> 00:00:03.253
it's November 6th,

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:05.380
the same day Will Byers goes missing

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.464
in the first episode,

00:00:06.464 --> 00:00:09.134
and Eleven opens a portal
to the Upside Down,

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:10.301
a parallel dimension

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:12.971
filled with unbelievable horrors.

00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:15.181
But what I still find kind of unbelieveable

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.850
is that there's some real science

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.728
to this notion of parallel worlds.

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:22.731
- Once you open up that curiosity door,

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:24.232
anything is possible.

00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:25.442
- [Narrator] But don't worry about them

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:27.193
being too much like the upside down,

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.154
because we'll probably never be able to

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:30.071
interact with them.

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:32.240
Hmm, probably.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.117
Here's how multiverse theory allows

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:36.703
for mind-blowing cosmic weirdness,

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:39.247
(suspenseful instrumental music)

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:41.332
and maybe even the parallel-dimensions

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:42.959
of "Stranger Things."

00:00:42.959 --> 00:00:46.588
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:51.843
(suspenseful instrumental music)

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:53.970
(pages turning)

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.263
- The Vale of Shadows

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:57.390
is a dimension that is a dark reflection

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.893
or echo of our world.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.394
- [Narrator] That's the
Dungeons and Dragons

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.645
version of the multiverse.

00:01:02.645 --> 00:01:04.814
And depending on which theory you use,

00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:08.193
it's honestly not that
far off from the science.

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:09.694
The theory of the multiverse

00:01:09.694 --> 00:01:12.197
is that our universe doesn't exist alone,

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:13.531
but is part of an ocean

00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:15.742
of unimaginably large expanses,

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.494
which may have different physical rules

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:19.079
from one another.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:19.996
And through the years,

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:21.539
different scientists have proposed

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:23.666
at least four theories of how we could be

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:25.210
one of many universes,

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.711
some of which get us closer

00:01:26.711 --> 00:01:28.213
to the Upside Down than others.

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:29.047
And while you'll need

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:30.548
a really good science teacher

00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:31.925
to understand the details,

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:32.967
the basics you can get,

00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:35.637
like why even start thinking about this?

00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:37.347
It's partly because scientists,

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:39.307
including the likes of Stephen Hawking

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:42.143
were troubled by how suspiciously perfect

00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:45.438
the conditions for life
are in our universe.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.356
Everywhere you look,

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:48.733
universal constants defy predictions

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:50.777
to fall within ranges that allow life,

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:53.113
like how--and I could
have found 15 examples

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.031
of this--specific quirks of carbon,

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:57.283
allow it to be abundant in our universe.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.369
The very building blocks of life.

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:03.248
For some the multiverse
is a potential solution

00:02:03.248 --> 00:02:05.250
to this and other problems.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.794
- So basically there
are parallel universes.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.629
- [Narrator] Think of clothes in a store.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.840
It might not make sense
to have a bright yellow

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.966
universe all alone,

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.592
but what if it were with an entire

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:15.802
multi-colored rack,

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.762
it starts to fit in more, right?

00:02:18.596 --> 00:02:20.348
That doesn't mean the
theories aren't weird,

00:02:20.348 --> 00:02:21.766
even the simplest version

00:02:21.766 --> 00:02:23.935
of the multiverse is weird.

00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:26.563
See models predict that
our universe is infinite.

00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:27.605
I know it's crazy,

00:02:27.605 --> 00:02:29.274
but matter can only arrange itself

00:02:29.274 --> 00:02:30.692
in so many ways.

00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:32.235
Imagine a deck of cards,

00:02:32.235 --> 00:02:34.445
any given card order may seem unique,

00:02:34.445 --> 00:02:35.864
but given enough shuffles,

00:02:35.864 --> 00:02:37.615
it will appear again.

00:02:37.615 --> 00:02:39.951
So our universe, too,

00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:42.370
could repeat itself
somewhere out in infinity,

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.497
beyond the limits of what we can now see.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.416
And that has strange implications

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:48.960
because not only will
there be an exact copy

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.296
of our Dustin in another
universe's version

00:02:51.296 --> 00:02:52.213
of "Stranger Things."

00:02:52.213 --> 00:02:55.133
There will be billions of mirror Dustins.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.759
- Mental.

00:02:56.759 --> 00:02:58.219
- Just like our world,

00:02:58.219 --> 00:03:00.471
but just infinite variations of it.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:03.808
- [Narrator] Some will
be small variations,

00:03:03.808 --> 00:03:05.518
maybe a different outfit in a scene.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.729
And sometimes they'll
become demodog breeders

00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:09.731
or start dating Nancy after their dance.

00:03:09.731 --> 00:03:12.859
Fan-fiction becomes real people.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.068
It stands to reason that

00:03:14.068 --> 00:03:15.570
in this infinite chowder,

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.572
pictured charmingly here in "Cosmos,"

00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:18.781
there could be a real world,

00:03:18.781 --> 00:03:21.075
which just happens to be exactly like

00:03:21.075 --> 00:03:22.160
the fictional Upside Down.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.369
(ominous instrumental music)

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.204
(alien chitter)

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.289
Even in our universe within the universe,

00:03:26.289 --> 00:03:29.000
scientists have proposed
that radioactive planets

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:29.876
would be capable

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:32.879
of sustaining very hardy lifeforms.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.797
(gunshots)

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:36.716
Of course your nearest identical twin

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.301
would be 10 to the 10,

00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:42.013
to the 118 meters
away--unimaginably far.

00:03:42.013 --> 00:03:43.723
So even if this theory is true,

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.849
the chances that they're going

00:03:44.849 --> 00:03:47.018
to bust through your wall are nil.

00:03:47.018 --> 00:03:48.311
(soft instrumental music)

00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:49.771
A different kind of multiverse

00:03:49.771 --> 00:03:52.190
is predicted by the theory
of cosmic inflation,

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.026
which isn't a fringe theory by the way.

00:03:55.026 --> 00:03:56.527
At the beginning of everything,

00:03:56.527 --> 00:03:58.613
the universe expanded far faster

00:03:58.613 --> 00:03:59.656
than the speed of light.

00:03:59.656 --> 00:04:03.159
It was an explosion of
space, not in space,

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:05.703
but that explosion wasn't uniform.

00:04:05.703 --> 00:04:07.580
Fluctuations meant that some parts

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.124
stopped inflating early
creating bubble universes

00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:12.752
like our own while other parts kept going.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:13.586
Scientists like to use

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.171
Swiss cheese for this,

00:04:15.171 --> 00:04:16.965
but this is a "Stranger Things" video

00:04:16.965 --> 00:04:18.508
so we're gonna use Dig Dug.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:21.511
These pockets patrolled by Pookas,

00:04:21.511 --> 00:04:23.554
and Fygars are universes.

00:04:23.554 --> 00:04:25.932
The soil is the space between universes,

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.017
which is rapidly inflating.

00:04:28.017 --> 00:04:29.102
Once bubbles form,

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:30.478
they get pushed farther apart

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:31.896
at faster than light speed.

00:04:31.896 --> 00:04:33.022
So under this theory,

00:04:33.022 --> 00:04:34.524
the Upside Down isn't likely

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:36.401
to come knocking either.

00:04:36.401 --> 00:04:37.819
The really weird part though,

00:04:37.819 --> 00:04:39.195
is that the bubble universes

00:04:39.195 --> 00:04:40.989
can have different laws of physics.

00:04:40.989 --> 00:04:43.992
So maybe transmuting hive-mind life forms

00:04:43.992 --> 00:04:46.119
are more likely there... possibly.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.037
Which leads us to the most controversial

00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:49.998
of all multiverses,

00:04:49.998 --> 00:04:52.083
but also maybe the most alluring.

00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:53.167
- You guys have been thinking

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:54.002
about Hugh Everett's,

00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:54.836
"Many Worlds Interpretation"

00:04:54.836 --> 00:04:55.670
haven't you?

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:56.504
- [Narrator] Yes!

00:04:56.504 --> 00:04:58.298
So far we've started from the big end

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.132
of the scale,

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.633
but the "Many Worlds Interpretation"

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.010
gets to the multiverse through

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.595
the smallest parts of existence.

00:05:04.595 --> 00:05:06.431
The big problem is that the physics

00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:10.184
of small stuff, quantum
mechanics is kooky,

00:05:10.184 --> 00:05:11.436
even physicists say

00:05:11.436 --> 00:05:13.646
they don't really understand it.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:16.274
One conundrum is how really small objects

00:05:16.274 --> 00:05:19.027
like photons behave in experiments.

00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:20.862
They appear to act as waves,

00:05:20.862 --> 00:05:23.156
multiple possible places at the same time

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:25.491
until we measure or observe them.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.910
Then all their possibilities collapse

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.078
into a particle.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.997
So the mere fact that we're looking

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:32.332
changes reality.

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:35.626
It causes an inanimate
insensate beam of light

00:05:35.626 --> 00:05:37.211
to make a choice.

00:05:37.211 --> 00:05:38.963
(air explosion)

00:05:39.047 --> 00:05:40.381
If you remember Schrodinger's cat,

00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:41.215
(cat meowing)

00:05:41.215 --> 00:05:42.425
that's what it's about.

00:05:42.425 --> 00:05:44.135
But scientists don't like this

00:05:44.135 --> 00:05:46.763
because it makes no sense.

00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:47.597
I mean,

00:05:47.597 --> 00:05:49.682
planets don't change
because we look at them,

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.517
the physicist, Hugh Everett III

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.853
had a simple yet mind-boggling

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.813
way out of this awkwardness.

00:05:55.813 --> 00:05:57.607
"The wave doesn't collapse."

00:05:57.607 --> 00:05:58.483
He said.

00:05:58.483 --> 00:06:00.318
We see one result here,

00:06:00.318 --> 00:06:02.904
but in other universes that split off

00:06:02.904 --> 00:06:03.738
from our own,

00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:06.657
other Uses see the other outcomes.

00:06:06.657 --> 00:06:08.326
An easier way to understand it

00:06:08.326 --> 00:06:09.786
might be through the telepathic,

00:06:09.786 --> 00:06:10.953
spin the bottle game

00:06:10.953 --> 00:06:13.873
that Max and Eleven
play in season three.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.166
While the bottle is spinning,

00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:17.251
there's a number of probable outcomes,

00:06:17.251 --> 00:06:20.713
but we all see it
collapse into one: Billy.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:21.547
But according

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:22.965
to the "Many Worlds Interpretation,"

00:06:22.965 --> 00:06:24.300
in another universe,

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.052
the bottle would tell other versions

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:28.679
of Eleven and Max to spy on Mr. Clarke

00:06:28.679 --> 00:06:30.264
or Steve or whoever.

00:06:30.264 --> 00:06:31.891
With universes branching off

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.434
at every quantum measurement

00:06:33.434 --> 00:06:34.685
creating infinite YOUs,

00:06:34.685 --> 00:06:37.522
it's suddenly crowded in here, right?

00:06:37.522 --> 00:06:40.191
Plus they all occupy
the same physical space

00:06:40.191 --> 00:06:41.150
at the same time,

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.194
sort of like the Upside Down does.

00:06:43.194 --> 00:06:45.655
But before you go taking
an axe to your walls,

00:06:45.655 --> 00:06:47.740
the universes are according to most,

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.325
completely sealed off from another

00:06:49.325 --> 00:06:50.410
after the split.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.620
(air swooshing)

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.163
And finally there's M-Theory.

00:06:54.163 --> 00:06:55.957
The most mind-boggling of all.

00:06:55.957 --> 00:06:58.042
Einstein spent the back half of his life

00:06:58.042 --> 00:07:01.254
looking for a grand
unifying theory of physics.

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:04.215
And some think they found it in M-Theory.

00:07:04.215 --> 00:07:06.384
It says that everything from quarks on up

00:07:06.384 --> 00:07:08.761
is composed of infinitely thin loops

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:11.180
vibrating at certain frequencies.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.350
But one peculiarity is that M-Theory

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.269
requires seven more dimensions

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:17.311
to work, dimensions

00:07:17.311 --> 00:07:19.063
which normal humans can't see,

00:07:19.063 --> 00:07:20.773
a concept helpfully explained

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:22.358
by Mr. Clark in the show.

00:07:22.358 --> 00:07:25.111
- Here's where things get really interesting.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:27.655
The flea can also travel this way along

00:07:27.655 --> 00:07:29.699
along the side of the rope.

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:33.744
He can even go underneath the rope.

00:07:33.744 --> 00:07:35.163
- [Narrator] But M-Theory also envisioned

00:07:35.163 --> 00:07:36.664
strings attaching to structures

00:07:36.664 --> 00:07:38.332
called branes like membranes,

00:07:38.332 --> 00:07:40.835
which we'll need special
help demonstrating.

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:43.004
You can think of them as multi-dimensional

00:07:43.004 --> 00:07:44.422
space waffles floating

00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:46.591
in stacks of higher dimensional syrupy

00:07:46.591 --> 00:07:48.634
space-time called the bulk.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.928
Branes hold universes including ours.

00:07:50.928 --> 00:07:52.638
And those other branes could actually

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:55.349
be traveling through
hyperspace mere millimeters

00:07:55.349 --> 00:07:56.934
from us theoretically,

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:58.769
they could interact with us.

00:07:58.769 --> 00:08:00.104
It would account for mysteries

00:08:00.104 --> 00:08:02.106
like the weakness of gravity for instance,

00:08:02.106 --> 00:08:04.442
as foreign branes siphoned particles away

00:08:04.442 --> 00:08:05.651
from our world.

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.737
If a neighboring brane
brushed up against us,

00:08:07.737 --> 00:08:09.113
it could even unleash something

00:08:09.113 --> 00:08:10.490
like the big bang.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:11.574
- Science is neat,

00:08:12.408 --> 00:08:15.161
but I'm afraid it's not very forgiving.

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:16.829
- [Narrator] So maybe this is the theory

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:19.081
we've been searching for after all?

00:08:19.081 --> 00:08:20.208
- But again.

00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:21.042
- This is all-

00:08:21.042 --> 00:08:22.210
- Theoretical.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:23.044
- [Narrator] Look.

00:08:23.044 --> 00:08:24.587
No one has successfully tested

00:08:24.587 --> 00:08:25.505
any of these theories.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:26.339
In fact,

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:28.925
some are criticized for being untestable,

00:08:28.925 --> 00:08:30.551
and therefore unscientific.

00:08:30.551 --> 00:08:32.136
So in the end multiverse theory

00:08:32.136 --> 00:08:33.804
is partly a thought exercise

00:08:33.804 --> 00:08:37.016
on the grand scale and
strangeness of the cosmos.

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:39.602
But still,

00:08:39.602 --> 00:08:41.395
if the Demogorgons do break through,

00:08:41.395 --> 00:08:42.813
don't say we didn't warn you.

00:08:42.813 --> 00:08:45.107
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:08:45.107 --> 00:08:45.983
Okay.

00:08:45.983 --> 00:08:47.693
I know I said that universes

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:50.238
in Hugh Everett's "Many Worlds Interpretation"

00:08:50.238 --> 00:08:51.989
wouldn't interact with each other,

00:08:51.989 --> 00:08:54.617
but some believe that quantum computers,

00:08:54.617 --> 00:08:57.119
the beginnings of which
we are already seeing

00:08:57.119 --> 00:08:59.080
actually get their otherworldly speed

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:01.874
because their calculations
are simultaneously

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:05.628
carried out in other universes.

00:09:05.628 --> 00:09:08.589
We hope you know what
you're doing scientists.

00:09:08.589 --> 00:09:12.009
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:09:12.009 --> 00:09:13.386
(alien roaring)

